(
  '11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111',
  'blog',
  'turkish-breakfast-san-francisco',
  'A Guide to Turkish Breakfast in San Francisco',
  'Learn how a traditional Turkish breakfast brings bread, cheeses, olives, eggs, tea and conversation together around one generous table.',
  '[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Turkish breakfast is less about one main dish and more about sharing a table filled with complementary flavors. Warm bread, savory cheeses, olives, vegetables, eggs, preserves, honey and tea arrive together, inviting everyone to taste, pass plates and stay a little longer."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"What makes a Turkish breakfast distinctive?"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The variety creates the experience. Salty cheese and olives balance sweet honey or preserves. Tomatoes and cucumbers bring freshness, while eggs and freshly baked breads make the meal substantial. Rather than moving through separate courses, guests build each bite according to taste."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Bread at the center of the table"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Bread connects the different parts of breakfast. It can carry cheese and herbs, gather a spoonful of egg, or pair with honey. Turkish bakeries also produce savory pastries such as borek, acma and pogaca, each offering a different texture and filling."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Tea, coffee and conversation"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Turkish tea is traditionally served throughout breakfast, keeping the table warm and social. Turkish coffee has its own place in the culture and is often enjoyed after food. Both drinks encourage a slower rhythm than a meal designed simply to be eaten on the way somewhere else."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Enjoy Turkish breakfast at Turquaz"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"At Turquaz in San Francisco, breakfast reflects the same spirit of abundance and gathering. Our menu brings Turkish flavors, bakery traditions and warm hospitality to 1198 Mission Street. Check the current menu for available breakfast dishes and pastries before your visit."},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["Explore the current Turquaz menu online","Reserve a table for breakfast with family or friends","Allow time to share several flavors together"]}]',
  'published',
  'Turkish Breakfast in San Francisco | Turquaz',
  'Discover Turkish breakfast traditions, tea, pastries and shared plates at Turquaz restaurant in San Francisco.',
  'https://www.turquazsf.com/assets/images/dish-feature.jpeg',
  'Turkish breakfast spread with eggs, cheeses, olives, honey and bread at Turquaz',
  'turkish breakfast san francisco',
  'Turquaz',
  '2026-08-20T16:00:00.000Z',
  '2026-08-20T16:00:00.000Z',
  '2026-08-20T16:00:00.000Z'
),
(
  '22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222',
  'blog',
  'turkish-dishes-and-ingredients',
  'Turkish Dishes and Ingredients to Know',
  'Explore the ingredients and cooking traditions behind meze, kebabs, pide, lentil soup, baklava and other Turkish favorites.',
  '[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Turkish cooking reflects many regions, climates and generations of home and restaurant kitchens. Vegetables, grains, legumes, yogurt, herbs, olive oil, grilled meats, breads and pastries appear in combinations that can feel both comforting and remarkably varied."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Start with meze"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Meze are small dishes made for sharing. Hummus, spicy ezme, yogurt-based dips, stuffed grape leaves, roasted eggplant and pickled vegetables can open a meal with contrasting textures and temperatures. Ordering several allows the table to experience a wider range of flavors."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Kebabs and the grill"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Turkish kebabs are not one single recipe. Adana kebab uses seasoned minced meat, while shish preparations place marinated pieces of meat or vegetables on skewers. Kofte are seasoned meatballs shaped for the grill. Each style depends on careful seasoning, heat and timing."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Pide, lahmacun and baked specialties"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Pide is a boat-shaped Turkish flatbread baked with toppings such as cheese, spinach or seasoned meat. Lahmacun is thinner and crisp, topped with a finely chopped savory mixture. Borek and other bakery items use layered or shaped doughs for flaky, tender results."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Everyday ingredients with depth"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":["Eggplant, tomatoes, peppers and leafy herbs","Lentils, chickpeas, rice and bulgur","Yogurt, cheeses and butter","Olive oil, lemon, sumac and warm spices","Pistachios, walnuts, honey and pastry"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discover the menu at Turquaz"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Turquaz menu in San Francisco includes cold and hot meze, soups and salads, bowls, grilled plates, flatbreads, bakery items, desserts and coffee. Availability and prices can change, so the live menu is the best source when planning your meal."}]',
  'published',
  'Turkish Dishes and Ingredients | Turquaz SF',
  'Learn about Turkish meze, kebabs, pide, lentils, yogurt, eggplant, baklava and more from Turquaz in San Francisco.',
  'https://www.turquazsf.com/assets/images/dish-feast.jpeg',
  'A shared table of Turkish meze, salads, bread and grilled dishes at Turquaz',
  'turkish dishes and ingredients',
