(
  '33333333-3333-4333-8333-333333333333',
  'blog',
  'turkish-coffee-and-tea-culture',
  'Turkish Coffee and Tea: A Culture of Hospitality',
  'Discover why Turkish coffee and tea are closely connected to hospitality, conversation and the rhythm of a shared meal.',
  '[{"type":"paragraph","text":"In Turkish hospitality, a hot drink is often an invitation to pause. Tea and coffee are served in different ways, yet both create space for conversation and connection before, during or after food."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Turkish tea throughout the day"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Turkish tea is commonly brewed strong and served in small, curved glasses. Guests can adjust its intensity and sweetness to taste. Refills make tea a companion to breakfast, a work break, an afternoon visit or an evening conversation."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"What makes Turkish coffee different?"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Turkish coffee is prepared from very finely ground coffee and served unfiltered in a small cup. The method creates a concentrated drink with a distinctive body. It is meant to be sipped slowly, allowing the grounds to settle at the bottom."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Coffee after a meal"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Because Turkish coffee is small and intense, it can provide a satisfying close to a meal. A sweet pastry such as baklava offers a complementary contrast, while a glass of water refreshes the palate."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Hospitality is the essential ingredient"},{"type":"quote","text":"The meaning of the cup comes from the welcome around it."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Methods and serving pieces matter, but hospitality gives both drinks their cultural role. Offering tea or coffee tells a guest that there is time for them. At Turquaz, coffee, bakery and dining come together in that same welcoming spirit."}]',
  'published',
  'Turkish Coffee and Tea Culture | Turquaz SF',
  'Learn how Turkish coffee and tea bring hospitality, conversation and tradition to the table at Turquaz in San Francisco.',
  'https://www.turquazsf.com/assets/images/gallery-2.jpeg',
  'Coffee and bar area inside Turquaz restaurant in San Francisco',
  'turkish coffee san francisco',
  'Turquaz',
  '2026-08-22T16:00:00.000Z',
  '2026-08-22T16:00:00.000Z',
  '2026-08-22T16:00:00.000Z'
),
(
  '44444444-4444-4444-8444-444444444444',
  'blog',
  'mission-district-dining-plan',
  'Planning a Meal Near San Francisco’s Mission District',
  'A practical guide to planning breakfast, lunch, dinner or a group meal near the Mission District and central San Francisco.',
  '[{"type":"paragraph","text":"A good San Francisco dining plan starts with the occasion. A quick lunch has different needs from a long family dinner, while a group gathering benefits from advance planning. Turquaz is located at 1198 Mission Street, close to the Civic Center side of the Mission corridor."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Choose the right time for your visit"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Breakfast offers a relaxed way to share pastries, eggs, tea and coffee. Lunch works well for bowls, salads, flatbreads and grilled plates. Dinner invites a broader spread of meze and dishes for the table. Review the current hours through the restaurant or its verified business listing before traveling."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Plan around the table"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"For a group, think about dietary preferences, how many dishes everyone wants to share and whether the occasion needs extra time. Turquaz serves a varied Turkish and Mediterranean menu with vegetable dishes, meze, salads, grilled plates, breads and desserts. Ask the restaurant directly about current ingredients and accommodations."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reserve before a busy meal period"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"A reservation helps the team prepare for your party and reduces uncertainty during popular periods. The Turquaz website accepts reservations for up to 15 guests. Larger groups can contact the restaurant by phone to discuss options."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Build a complete San Francisco outing"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The central location makes it possible to pair a meal with nearby arts, culture, shopping or an event. Check transit and venue information on the day of your visit because schedules and street conditions can change."},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":["Review the live menu","Confirm current hours","Reserve for your party size","Allow time for shared dishes and dessert"]}]',
  'published',
  'Mission District Dining Plan | Turquaz San Francisco',
  'Plan breakfast, lunch, dinner or a group meal near San Francisco’s Mission District at Turquaz on Mission Street.',
